==English==
{{wikipedia|Get a life (idiom)}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-get a life.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|get<,,got,got[UK]:gotten[US]> a life}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive|derogatory|dismissal}} To begin having a more [[interesting]], [[eventful]], or [[worthwhile]] [[existence]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Sept 14 1995|author={{w|Joseph Berger (author)|Joseph Berger}}|titleurl=http://www.nytimes.com/1995/09/14/nyregion/disgraced-ex-lawman-in-rockland-avoids-jail.html|title=Disgraced, Ex-Lawman In Rockland Avoids Jail|journal=New York Times|accessdate=23 Aug 2016
|passage="He's really broken. Hopefully he'll be able to find work somewhere and '''get a life'''."}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=Dec 25 2006|author=w:Lev Grossman|title=Power To The People: Harriet Klausner, The Constant Critic|titleurl=http://content.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,1570816-6,00.html|journal=Time|accessdate=23 Aug 2016
|passage="Harriet, please '''get a life'''," someone begged her on a message board, "and leave us poor Amazon customers alone."}}

====Usage notes====
* Most often used in the [[imperative]], as a derogatory dismissal addressed to someone considered [[stuffy]], [[tedious]], or excessively [[nosy]]. Also, not to be confused with the idiomatic expression ''[[get life]]'', which has a different meaning.

